# CODEOWNERS: review routing, set by the project lead.
#
# How GitHub reads it: for every changed file, ONE approval from ANY listed owner satisfies the
# rule, and the PR author's own approval never counts. The last matching rule wins, so the most
# specific rules are at the bottom. Every owner needs write access to the repository.
#
# Two rules follow from that, and are why most paths below list two people:
#   1. A path owned only by its author could never be merged (the ruleset has no bypass actors).
#      So every path has an owner other than the person who usually writes it.
#   2. It cannot demand two people. "Two reviewers" for RatelLink and RatelBSS: money is enforced
#      by .github/workflows/critical-review-gate.yml using .github/critical-paths.txt and
#      .github/critical-reviewers.txt. See docs/GITHUB_SETUP.md and docs/adr/0004.
#
# Roles and the reasoning: docs/TEAM_STRUCTURE.md and docs/OWNERSHIP_MATRIX.md.

# Default: the project lead, or the second senior developer when the lead is the author.
